Found by the k134 worker; on HEAD too. (1) User-visible: hermes-setup refuses any Hermes config that holds, anywhere in the file, a folded block scalar with a more-indented line, or a literal block scalar that starts with a blank line. The vendored yaml.v3 (v3.0.1) writes these back differently, so checkEdit refuses with 'the result would change more than mcp_servers.unreagent' and names neither the key nor the cause. Fix: name the cause and the offending key, or splice the new entry into the original text instead of re-encoding. Note: k134's TestHermesSetupChecksTheEditBeforeWriting uses exactly this quirk to reach checkEdit, so fixing (1) needs another input for that test. (2) Contrived: plainMergeKeys turns a quoted, tagged merge key (!!merge "<<") into a plain string key; only checkEdit catches it. (3) Contrived: an entry key with a non-string tag (!!binary for url) is missed, so a second url is added and the old one wins; only checkEdit catches it. Lane: unreagent-worker.

